{
  "_doc": "Looks are per type and can be mapped per planet: \"planets\" maps a planet id onto a look type (\"frost_moon\": \"ice_moon\") or a type with overrides ({\"look\": \"ice_moon\", \"landmark\": \"gantry\"}); a world record's \"look\" key names one (WorldLook.look_for_planet). [worlds2] How each Cradle Mode world type looks (systems/world_look.gd, planet/world_look_view.gd). grade: the sky and fog grade over the planet's own haze (planet/sky_director.gd, the same keys as data/frontiers.json grade); it eases off by restore_ease as the district is restored, so a world starts in its own weather and clears toward bright air without losing its identity. dust: a light dust storm amount that clears with restoration. sky_body: a big body in the sky (kind ringed | moon | shattered; size = angular size of the billboard in degrees, yaw/elev in degrees, twin = a second small moon). city: tint multiplies building and skyline facade colours; weather is the weathering overlay on the city (art/shaders/world_weather.gdshader: top = cover on up faces, film = everywhere, low = a band rising from the ground, streak = vertical streaks under ledges). dress: the base yard (planet/street_dressing.gd: drift amount and colour, awning bleach, puddle count). landmark: one big silhouette per world type out past the city (planet/world_landmark.gd). Modifiers add on top: long_nights darkens nights, heavy_rain doubles puddles and wets the junk, rich_salvage makes the junk shine.",
